  "verdict": "Q51451's domain-start hypothesis is REFUTED: UniProt puts the ADP-RT domain at 243-429, not at 234. The real defect is larger than the open item named, because the entry omits UniProt sites [186, 187, 319, 343] while agreeing on [146, 381]. Its ratio stays below 1.0 under all 4 annotations tested, so ExoS is robust. \ud83d\udd34 P01552 is NOT. Offset 0 is DISPROVEN: positions [23, 25] fall inside the cleaved signal peptide, where a secreted superantigen's receptor interface cannot be. The only frame consistent with UniProt's signal peptide and its 93-113 mature disulfide is +27, and there the ratio goes 0.9556 -> 1.0417, crossing 1.0. So SEB's contribution to the published 13/15 rests on a coordinate frame that is ruled out. Re-curation stays OPEN because UniProt annotates no site features for SEB at all, so no annotation meeting this project's own offset-acceptance test exists for it.",
